      "role": "user",
      "content": "These are a good start, but they feel a bit archetypal. I really want this to feel grounded in a specific, modern metropolis—think a place like Chicago or New York. Can you make these characters more specific? I'm talking about their actual backgrounds, ethnicities, and how their cultural identity plays into their role in the underworld. It'll help me write more authentic dialogue and tension. For example, what kind of specific ethnic or neighborhood backgrounds would make these guys feel like they actually belong in those gritty street-level scenes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
